.TH "REPROCTL\-SETUP" "1" "2026" "reproctl" "Repro Development Tools"
.SH NAME
reproctl\-setup \- bootstrap the local development environment
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]reproctl setup\f[R] [\f[B]\-\-skip\-cluster\f[R]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Runs a 9\-step bootstrap sequence to prepare the local development
environment:
.IP "1." 3
\f[B]brew bundle\f[R] \(em install Homebrew dependencies from the
Brewfile.
.IP "2." 3
\f[B]agent\-browser runtime\f[R] \(em verify the CLI is installed and
provision the shared Chrome for Testing runtime with
\f[CR]agent\-browser install\f[R] when needed.
.IP "3." 3
\f[B]direnv check\f[R] \(em verify the direnv shell hook is active.
.IP "4." 3
\f[B]proto use\f[R] \(em activate the correct toolchain versions.
.IP "5." 3
\f[B]pnpm install\f[R] \(em install Node.js dependencies.
.IP "6." 3
\f[B]Docker check\f[R] \(em verify Docker is running.
.IP "7." 3
\f[B]direnv allow\f[R] \(em trust the \f[CR].envrc\f[R] file.
.IP "8." 3
\f[B].envrc.local\f[R] \(em write \f[CR].envrc.local\f[R] exporting
\f[CR]OPENCODE_CONFIG_CONTENT\f[R] with agent permissions scoped to the
local checkout parent directory (covers all sibling worktrees).
Loaded by direnv via \f[CR]source_env_if_exists\f[R].
This file is gitignored and regenerated on every run.
.IP "9." 3
\f[B]cluster up\f[R] \(em create the local kind cluster and container
registry.
.PP
Each step is idempotent and safe to re\-run.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\f[B]\-\-skip\-cluster\f[R]
Skip step 9 (kind cluster creation).
Useful when you only need to update dependencies without touching the
cluster.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
reproctl setup
Run the full bootstrap sequence.
.TP
reproctl setup \-\-skip\-cluster
Bootstrap without creating the cluster.
